{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Of the fowl.</b> And not every fowl — for it says ״תָּמִים זָכָר בַּבָּקָר בַּכְּשָׂבִים וּבָעִזִּים״ — wholeness and maleness in animals, but there is no wholeness and maleness in birds — one might say even one missing a limb; therefore it says ״מִן הָעוֹף״ (there)." "<b>Turtledoves.</b> Large ones, and not small ones." "<b>Young pigeons.</b> Small ones, and not large ones." "<b>Of the turtledoves or of the young pigeons.</b> To exclude the onset of yellowing in these and those, which is disqualified — because it is large among young pigeons and small among turtledoves (Ḥulin 22)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:39.533223881Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}